Article 5: For an insurance contract concluded before the Insurance Law comes into force, the time periods under the following circumstances shall be calculated from October 1, 2009:
(1) Where, before the Insurance Law comes into force, the insurer received a request for compensation or payment of insurance benefits, and after the Insurance Law comes into force, the thirty-day period provided for in Article 23 of the Insurance Law shall apply;
(2) Where, before the Insurance Law comes into force, the insurer became aware of the grounds for dissolution, and after the Insurance Law comes into force, the insurer exercises the right of dissolution in accordance with Articles 16 and 32 of the Insurance Law, the thirty-day period provided for in Article 16 of the Insurance Law shall apply;
(3) Where, after the Insurance Law comes into force, the insurer requests dissolution of the contract in accordance with paragraph 2 of Article 16 of the Insurance Law, the two-year period provided for in Article 16 of the Insurance Law shall apply;
(4) Where, before the Insurance Law comes into force, the insurer received notice of the transfer of the subject matter insured, and after the Insurance Law comes into force, requests an increase of the insurance premium or dissolution of the contract in accordance with the contract on the grounds that the transfer of the subject matter insured significantly increased the degree of risk, the thirty-day period provided for in Article 49 of the Insurance Law shall apply.
